From 5052a3ad2d12e97437a63574393287729841f2e5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Keith Packard <keithp@keithp.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 07:04:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 19/19] test-posix: Check the <ctype.h> and <wctype.h> _l
 functions

Check that every <ctype.h> _l function, as a macro and as a function,
gives the POSIX locale's classes and case mappings (XBD 7.3.1.1) for
EOF and every byte, with only cntrl and punct allowed outside the
portable characters, and that <ctype.h> takes application macros
named like its parameters. Check wctype_l, wctrans_l, iswctype_l and
towctrans_l, including (wctype_t)0 and (wctrans_t)0, the isw*_l and
tow*_l functions and WEOF. With picolibc's ISO-8859-1 and C.UTF-8
locales, check that the _l functions follow their argument and the
others the thread's locale.
